<p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / JESSE KOEPPEL</p>
<h1>Engineering across disciplines.</h1>
<div class="prose">
<p>I study mechanical engineering at Washington University in St. Louis and lead suspension engineering at WashU Racing. Outside the team, I develop vehicle dynamics simulation tools and quantitative research systems.</p>
<p>I’m particularly interested in the point where a mathematical model meets a physical measurement: building tools that make the assumptions clear, testing them against independent evidence, and using the results to guide a design decision.</p>
<h2>Education and experience</h2>
<p>I expect to graduate in May 2028. At WashU Racing, I headed both the WUFR-26 and WUFR-27 steering final design reviews, with responsibility for the design, manufacture and integration of the steering system and broader suspension engineering.</p>
